oso's change to libghostty-vt 1.0.1 (MIT, like the library), applied by build.rs after
0001 and 0003 and checked against ghostty-vt.lock: a column reflow that cannot fit a
cell's hyperlink, grapheme or style into a page, even after growing the page to its
maximum capacity, drops that data and keeps the cell, in every build, instead of
crashing in safe builds. A dense page narrowed reaches this, and a live terminal
reflows the same way. Drop or rebase it at every bump.

diff -ruN a/src/terminal/PageList.zig b/src/terminal/PageList.zig
--- a/src/terminal/PageList.zig
+++ b/src/terminal/PageList.zig
@@ -2495,10 +2495,11 @@
                 // though we choose to recover by corrupting the cell
                 // to a non-grapheme codepoint.
                 log.err("setGraphemes failed after capacity increase err={}", .{err});
-                if (comptime std.debug.runtime_safety) {
-                    // Force a crash with safe builds.
-                    unreachable;
-                }
+                // oso patch: a reflow can exhaust this page's capacity for the
+                // cell's managed memory (a hyperlink/grapheme/style-dense page
+                // narrowed) even at the maximum, which a live terminal reflows
+                // the same way. Degrade by dropping it (below) in every build
+                // instead of crashing in safe builds.
 
                 // Unsafe builds we throw away grapheme data!
                 self.page_cell.content_tag = .codepoint;
@@ -2531,10 +2532,11 @@
                 // This shouldn't fail since we did a capacity
                 // check above.
                 log.err("link dupe failed with capacity check err={}", .{err});
-                if (comptime std.debug.runtime_safety) {
